\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Last year me & @kevinafischer were on a drive down to @DisneyLand exploring the acquisition of my company @LingonberryHQ. At a coffee shop half way, we decided we should create a character who would be impossible for our investors and friends to resist loving. Through many years of producing art, I learned people tend to drastically love things when they see themselves in the art. \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Spark took his name from one of our investors, @SparkCapital. Their mascot was already a dog, but it had no rizz. A very serious drawing of a creature who is warm and friendly. \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Warmth comes from the inside not the outside. I spent many months getting inside Spark\'92 head. I spent time in Portugal studying character psychology from one of the legendary acting consultants and masterclass teachers of Pixar.  \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Spark was designed inside out under my direction. I brought in my friend @JaredChapman to create the original model drawings. My other friend Tony Mora translated him into the 3D ready for animation model. Will Anderson was the Technical Director.  There are also a number of other technicians and artists who have contributed to Spark. That\'92s why he has a strong spirit. \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
