\f0\b Goal
\f1\b0 \
Create a local web app that takes a batch of mostly iPhone portrait videos and automatically finds multiple interesting segments, then exports a TikTok-ready vertical edit no longer than 60 seconds, with a strong hook in the first few seconds.\
\

\f0\b High level behavior
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	\'95	User selects one or more portrait iPhone videos from their machine\
	\'95	For each input video, the app finds several \'93interesting\'94 segments (not just one)\
	\'95	The app then either:\
	\'95	Exports a 60s or shorter highlight reel per input video, or\
	\'95	Exports one combined 60s or shorter supercut that pulls segments from all inputs\
	\'95	Everything runs locally on my machine, no cloud calls\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 TikTok hook optimization
\f1\b0 \
The main objective is to maximize the first 3 to 5 seconds as a hook. For v1, use heuristics like:\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	\'95	Prefer segments that start with:\
	\'95	A spike in audio energy (sudden speech, laughter, exclamation, sound effect, music drop)\
	\'95	A visual change (cut, camera move, subject entering frame)\
	\'95	Penalize segments that start with:\
	\'95	Silence or very low audio energy\
	\'95	Static or boring frames (no motion, no subject)\
	\'95	When building the final 60s edit:\
	\'95	Rank all segments globally by \'93hook score\'94\
	\'95	Force the highest scoring segment to be placed first in the timeline\
	\'95	Fill the remaining time with other high scoring segments in a sensible order\
	\'95	Optionally keep a minimum hook duration (for example 2 to 5 seconds) so the opening beat has time to land\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \'93Interesting\'94 segment rules (overall)
\f1\b0 \
Use simple heuristics that we can refine later:\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	\'95	Audio based\
	\'95	Use loudness and sudden changes to find high energy moments\
	\'95	Favor speech, laughter, crowd noise, music\
	\'95	Avoid long silence\
	\'95	Visual based (lightweight)\
	\'95	Simple motion or scene change detection\
	\'95	Avoid black frames, totally blown out or extremely blurry sections\
	\'95	Segment selection\
	\'95	Detect several candidate windows per video\
	\'95	Rank by a score that combines hook potential and overall energy\
	\'95	Choose top N segments per video that fit inside a 60 second cap for the final edit\
	\'95	Per segment min and max duration (for example 2 to 15 seconds, configurable)\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 TikTok / format specifics
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	\'95	Assume input is mostly iPhone footage in portrait (9:16)\
	\'95	Output:\
	\'95	9:16 vertical video\
	\'95	Ready to upload directly to TikTok and Reels\
	\'95	Sensible defaults for codec and bitrate suitable for TikTok\
	\'95	If an input is not 9:16, center crop or pillarbox to fit a 9:16 frame\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 UI requirements
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	\'95	Local desktop app on macOS\
	\'95	Dark themed UI\
	\'95	Main screen elements:\
	\'95	File picker to add one or more video files\
	\'95	List view of selected videos with:\
	\'95	Filename\
	\'95	Status (queued, analyzing, selecting segments, exporting, done, error)\
	\'95	Per video progress bar\
	\'95	Global progress bar for the whole batch\
	\'95	Scrollable log console that streams pipeline messages in real time\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Logging and transparency
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	\'95	Live log panel that prints each step, for example:\
	\'95	\'93Loading video X.mov\'94\
	\'95	\'93Extracting audio waveform\'94\
	\'95	\'93Detecting high energy regions\'94\
	\'95	\'93Found 4 candidate segments\'94\
	\'95	\'93Top segment chosen as hook: 00:03.2 to 00:07.9\'94\
	\'95	\'93Selected 3 segments total duration 52.4s\'94\
	\'95	\'93Exporting highlight reel to /output/X_highlight.mp4\'94\
	\'95	Also write logs to a local file per run for debugging\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Pipeline sketch
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	\'95	For each input video:\
	\'95	Load video and extract audio and basic motion or scene change info\
	\'95	Generate candidate segments around high energy areas\
	\'95	Score candidates for:\
	\'95	Hook potential (how strong the first moments are)\
	\'95	Overall interestingness (audio + motion)\
	\'95	Pick top segments that fit within a 60 second cap and respect min / max segment length\
	\'95	Global assembly stage:\
	\'95	Depending on mode, either:\
	\'95	Build one reel per video, or\
	\'95	Build one combined supercut from all segments\
	\'95	Always place the highest scoring segment first as the hook\
	\'95	Use hard cuts between segments for v1\
	\'95	Export final 9:16 clip and update the UI and logs\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Quality of life and config
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	\'95	Support MP4 and MOV at minimum\
	\'95	Clear error messages per file in both the list view and the log console\
	\'95	Simple configuration panel:\
	\'95	Target total clip length (default 60 seconds)\
	\'95	Per segment min and max duration\
	\'95	Toggle between \'93one reel per source video\'94 and \'93single combined supercut\'94\
	\'95	Output folder selector\
\
Main priority: local processing, clear dark UI with visible progress, multiple interesting segments per video, and a TikTok optimized edit where the very first seconds are the strongest possible hook.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
